     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. A single 1,700 mg dose is also above the typical maximum per dose of about 850 mg to 1,000 mg. Doses this high raise the risk of serious GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nCould you check the intended dose? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release metformin.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **A different drug or formulation**, or a typo.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and tell me the clinical reason. I'd add that to the order note."
      }
